<main>
    <header class="page-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Component reference</p>
        <h1>Options and API</h1>
        <p class="intro">Reference for option data, configuration, events, and keyboard behavior.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="content-card" aria-labelledby="option-shape-heading">
        <h2 id="option-shape-heading">Option shape</h2>
        <p>Every option needs a string or numeric <code>value</code> (or <code>valeur</code>) and a string <code>label</code>. Optional <code>icon</code> values accept Web Awesome icon names or descriptors in the form <code>{name, family?, variant?}</code>, SVG/PNG URL strings, or image descriptors in the form <code>{src, fallback?}</code>. The fallback text appears if the image cannot load. Other properties, such as <code>department</code>, <code>region</code>, and <code>country</code>, are preserved as option metadata.</p>
        <pre data-language="JSON"><code>{
  <span class="token-property">"value"</span>: <span class="token-string">"paris"</span>,
  <span class="token-property">"label"</span>: <span class="token-string">"Paris"</span>,
  <span class="token-property">"icon"</span>: <span class="token-string">"location-dot"</span>,
  <span class="token-property">"department"</span>: <span class="token-string">"75"</span>,
  <span class="token-property">"region"</span>: <span class="token-string">"Île-de-France"</span>,
  <span class="token-property">"country"</span>: <span class="token-string">"France"</span>
}</code></pre>
    </section>

    <section class="content-card" aria-labelledby="local-options-heading">
        <h2 id="local-options-heading">Local options</h2>
        <p>Provide local choices in either HTML or JavaScript. Direct <code>wa-option</code> children are read as the initial list. Assigning an array to <code>field.options</code> is useful for generated data and replaces any child options on that field. Visible suggestions are rendered with Web Awesome <code>wa-option</code> elements, including results from remote search.</p>
        <h3>Static choices with <code>wa-option</code></h3>
        <p>Set <code>value</code> on each child. Its trimmed text becomes the visible label unless a <code>label</code> attribute is provided. Use <code>data-icon</code> for an icon and other <code>data-*</code> attributes for string metadata; dashed names become camel-case keys on the option.</p>
        <pre data-language="HTML"><code><span class="token-punctuation">&lt;</span><span class="token-tag">lgs1920-autocomplete</span> <span class="token-attribute">id</span>=<span class="token-attribute-value">"markup-city-search"</span> <span class="token-attribute">label</span>=<span class="token-attribute-value">"City"</span> <span class="token-attribute">name</span>=<span class="token-attribute-value">"city"</span><span class="token-punctuation">&gt;</span>
  <span class="token-punctuation">&lt;</span><span class="token-tag">wa-option</span> <span class="token-attribute">value</span>=<span class="token-attribute-value">"paris"</span> <span class="token-attribute">data-icon</span>=<span class="token-attribute-value">"location-dot"</span> <span class="token-attribute">data-department</span>=<span class="token-attribute-value">"75"</span> <span class="token-attribute">data-region</span>=<span class="token-attribute-value">"Île-de-France"</span> <span class="token-attribute">data-country</span>=<span class="token-attribute-value">"France"</span><span class="token-punctuation">&gt;</span>Paris<span class="token-punctuation">&lt;/</span><span class="token-tag">wa-option</span><span class="token-punctuation">&gt;</span>
  <span class="token-punctuation">&lt;</span><span class="token-tag">wa-option</span> <span class="token-attribute">value</span>=<span class="token-attribute-value">"reims"</span> <span class="token-attribute">data-icon</span>=<span class="token-attribute-value">"city"</span> <span class="token-attribute">data-department</span>=<span class="token-attribute-value">"51"</span> <span class="token-attribute">data-region</span>=<span class="token-attribute-value">"Grand Est"</span> <span class="token-attribute">data-country</span>=<span class="token-attribute-value">"France"</span><span class="token-punctuation">&gt;</span>Reims<span class="token-punctuation">&lt;/</span><span class="token-tag">wa-option</span><span class="token-punctuation">&gt;</span>
<span class="token-punctuation">&lt;/</span><span class="token-tag">lgs1920-autocomplete</span><span class="token-punctuation">&gt;</span></code></pre>
        <h3>JavaScript-managed choices</h3>
        <p>Use an empty autocomplete element when the list comes from JavaScript. Each object uses the same option shape, and its additional fields remain available in the selected option and selection events.</p>
        <pre data-language="HTML"><code><span class="token-punctuation">&lt;</span><span class="token-tag">lgs1920-autocomplete</span> <span class="token-attribute">id</span>=<span class="token-attribute-value">"js-city-search"</span> <span class="token-attribute">label</span>=<span class="token-attribute-value">"City"</span> <span class="token-attribute">name</span>=<span class="token-attribute-value">"city"</span><span class="token-punctuation">&gt;&lt;/</span><span class="token-tag">lgs1920-autocomplete</span><span class="token-punctuation">&gt;</span></code></pre>
        <pre data-language="JavaScript"><code><span class="token-keyword">const</span> field = document.querySelector(<span class="token-string">'#js-city-search'</span>)
field.options = [
  {<span class="token-property">value</span>: <span class="token-string">'paris'</span>, <span class="token-property">label</span>: <span class="token-string">'Paris'</span>, <span class="token-property">icon</span>: <span class="token-string">'location-dot'</span>, <span class="token-property">department</span>: <span class="token-string">'75'</span>, <span class="token-property">region</span>: <span class="token-string">'Île-de-France'</span>, <span class="token-property">country</span>: <span class="token-string">'France'</span>},
  {<span class="token-property">value</span>: <span class="token-string">'reims'</span>, <span class="token-property">label</span>: <span class="token-string">'Reims'</span>, <span class="token-property">icon</span>: <span class="token-string">'city'</span>, <span class="token-property">department</span>: <span class="token-string">'51'</span>, <span class="token-property">region</span>: <span class="token-string">'Grand Est'</span>, <span class="token-property">country</span>: <span class="token-string">'France'</span>},
]</code></pre>
    </section>

    <section class="content-card" aria-labelledby="properties-heading">
        <h2 id="properties-heading">Properties and attributes</h2>
        <p>Use the listed names as HTML attributes. In JavaScript, hyphenated attribute names become camel-case properties, such as <code>max-options-visible</code> and <code>maxOptionsVisible</code>.</p>
        <div class="table-scroll table-scroll--wide" role="region" aria-label="Properties and attributes" tabindex="0">
            <table>
                <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td><code>options</code></td><td>Option[] property</td><td><code>[]</code></td><td>Local suggestions. Direct <code>wa-option</code> children provide initial choices; assigning this property replaces them and supports JavaScript-managed data. Matching checks <code>label</code> and <code>value</code>, without case sensitivity, and highlights matching text in labels. When recent suggestions are open, the disclosure chevron replaces them with the complete local list and points up. Activate it again to close the list. With an empty query and no recent suggestions, the chevron opens the full list directly. With <code>multiple</code>, options can be toggled without closing it.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>renderOption</code></td><td>Function property</td><td><code>null</code></td><td>Synchronous renderer <code>(option, {query}) =&gt; Node</code> for custom suggestion content. It replaces the default label rendering; <code>option.label</code> remains the search text, selected input text, and accessible name. Option icons still follow <code>icon-position</code>. Return a fresh, non-interactive DOM node for each suggestion; set to <code>null</code> to restore the default label view.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>optionTemplate</code> / <code>option-template</code></td><td>HTML template property / template ID attribute</td><td><code>null</code></td><td>Selects an HTML template for custom suggestion content, either by assigning the template element or its ID in the attribute. Declare the template before the autocomplete element. It replaces the default label rendering and query highlighting; <code>option.label</code> still controls matching, selected text, and the accessible name. Text-node placeholders use <code>{% raw %}{{field}}{% endraw %}</code> syntax and dot-separated paths; values are inserted as plain text. Setting either renderer clears the other.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>searchOptions</code></td><td>Function property</td><td><code>null</code></td><td>Async provider <code>(query, {signal}) =&gt; Promise&lt;Option[]&gt;</code>. Setting it enables remote search.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>persistence</code></td><td><code>{id?, group?, limit}</code> property</td><td><code>null</code></td><td>Requires an <code>id</code> or a <code>group</code>. Saves the last selected options under an id-specific key, or under a shared group key when <code>group</code> is set. Components with the same group share their recent history. <code>count</code> aliases <code>limit</code>.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>value</code></td><td>String, number, or array property</td><td><code>''</code> or <code>[]</code></td><td>Raw selected value. With <code>multiple</code>, this is an array. Setting it selects matching options already available to the component; it does not start a remote search.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>query</code></td><td>Read-only string property</td><td><code>''</code></td><td>Current text in the input, including while the user is typing an unselected query.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>selectedOption</code></td><td>Read-only <code>Option</code> or <code>null</code> property</td><td><code>null</code></td><td>The selected object in single mode; use <code>selectedOptions</code> in multiple mode.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>selectedOptions</code></td><td>Read-only Option[] property</td><td><code>[]</code></td><td>All selected option objects, including host-owned metadata. In single mode it contains zero or one option.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>focus()</code></td><td>Method</td><td>—</td><td>Focus the underlying Web Awesome input.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>label</code></td><td>String attribute/property</td><td><code>''</code></td><td>Accessible visible label forwarded to <code>wa-input</code>.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>placeholder</code></td><td>String attribute/property</td><td><code>''</code></td><td>Hint displayed while the query is empty and, in multiple mode, no options are selected.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>name</code></td><td>String attribute/property</td><td><code>''</code></td><td>Form field name for selected values. Multiple selection submits repeated entries under this name.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>disabled</code></td><td>Boolean attribute/property</td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Disables the input and excludes its value from form submission.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>with-clear</code></td><td>Boolean attribute / <code>withClear</code> property</td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Adds an accessible query-clear control. In multiple mode, a separate button clears all selected tags.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>multiple</code></td><td>Boolean attribute/property</td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Allows several options to be selected. Adding an option clears the current query and keeps the panel open. Local search shows the complete list; remote search keeps its current results available until the next query. The placeholder stays hidden while tags are selected. Values are submitted as repeated form entries under the same <code>name</code>.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>max-options-visible</code></td><td>Non-negative number attribute / <code>maxOptionsVisible</code> property</td><td><code>5</code></td><td>Maximum selected tags shown before a <code>+N</code> control opens the full selection list, paginated 10 items per page. Set to <code>0</code> to show every tag inline.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>size</code></td><td><code>xs</code>, <code>s</code>, <code>m</code>, <code>l</code>, <code>xl</code></td><td><code>m</code></td><td>Forwards the Web Awesome input size. The <code>small</code>, <code>medium</code>, and <code>large</code> aliases are also supported.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>appearance</code></td><td><code>filled</code>, <code>outlined</code>, or <code>filled-outlined</code></td><td><code>outlined</code></td><td>Forwards the Web Awesome input appearance.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>pill</code></td><td>Boolean attribute/property</td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Forwards pill-style rounding to the Web Awesome input.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>hint</code></td><td>String attribute/property</td><td><code>''</code></td><td>Forwards hint text to the Web Awesome input.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>readonly</code></td><td>Boolean attribute/property</td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Makes the query field read-only while keeping suggestions selectable.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>icon-position</code></td><td>Attribute / <code>iconPosition</code> property: <code>start</code> or <code>end</code></td><td><code>start</code></td><td>Places each option icon before or after its label in suggestions and, in multiple mode, selected tags.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>min-chars</code></td><td>Number attribute / <code>minChars</code> property</td><td><code>1</code></td><td>Minimum non-empty query length before invoking the async provider. Set to <code>0</code> to allow any non-empty query; an empty query never invokes the provider.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>debounce</code></td><td>Milliseconds attribute/property</td><td><code>150</code></td><td>Wait after the latest keystroke before invoking the async provider. New input restarts the delay and aborts any stale request.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>page-size</code></td><td>Positive number attribute / <code>pageSize</code> property</td><td><code>10</code></td><td>Suggestions shown per page. When more than one page is available, a compact footer shows the current result range and a compact page counter with previous/next controls.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>max-results</code></td><td>Positive number attribute / <code>maxResults</code> property</td><td><code>50</code></td><td>Maximum filtered local or remote results. Opening the complete local list from the disclosure chevron includes every option.</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-card" aria-labelledby="custom-rendering-heading">
        <h2 id="custom-rendering-heading">Custom suggestion content</h2>
        <p>Set <code>renderOption</code> to return a fresh DOM node for each suggestion. This example renders location metadata in a <code>wa-card</code>. The option label still controls searching, the selected input value, and the accessible option name; custom content does not receive the default query highlighting.</p>
        <pre data-language="JavaScript"><code>field.renderOption = option <span class="token-operator">=&gt;</span> {
  <span class="token-keyword">const</span> card = document.createElement(<span class="token-string">'wa-card'</span>)
  card.setAttribute(<span class="token-string">'appearance'</span>, <span class="token-string">'outlined'</span>)
  <span class="token-keyword">for</span> (<span class="token-keyword">const</span> [label, value] <span class="token-keyword">of</span> [
    [<span class="token-string">'City'</span>, option.city],
    [<span class="token-string">'Department'</span>, option.department],
    [<span class="token-string">'Region'</span>, option.region],
    [<span class="token-string">'Country'</span>, option.country],
  ]) {
    <span class="token-keyword">if</span> (!value) <span class="token-keyword">continue</span>
    <span class="token-keyword">const</span> line = document.createElement(<span class="token-string">'div'</span>)
    line.textContent = <span class="token-string">`${label}: ${value}`</span>
    card.append(line)
  }
  <span class="token-keyword">return</span> card
}</code></pre>
        <p>For layouts that only need markup and field insertions, use an HTML template. It replaces the default label rendering and query highlighting. Put <code>{% raw %}{{field}}{% endraw %}</code> placeholders in text nodes; dot-separated paths are supported, and values are inserted as plain text. Reference the template ID with <code>option-template</code>, or assign it through <code>field.optionTemplate</code> when configuring the field in JavaScript.</p>
        <pre data-language="HTML"><code>{% raw %}&lt;template id="city-option-template"&gt;
  &lt;wa-card appearance="outlined"&gt;
    &lt;strong&gt;{{city}}&lt;/strong&gt;
    &lt;small&gt;{{region}} · {{country}}&lt;/small&gt;
  &lt;/wa-card&gt;
&lt;/template&gt;

&lt;lgs1920-autocomplete id="templated-city-search" label="City" option-template="city-option-template"&gt;&lt;/lgs1920-autocomplete&gt;{% endraw %}</code></pre>
        <pre data-language="JavaScript"><code>const field = document.querySelector(<span class="token-string">'#templated-city-search'</span>)
field.options = [
  {value: <span class="token-string">'paris'</span>, label: <span class="token-string">'Paris'</span>, city: <span class="token-string">'Paris'</span>, region: <span class="token-string">'Île-de-France'</span>, country: <span class="token-string">'France'</span>},
  {value: <span class="token-string">'reims'</span>, label: <span class="token-string">'Reims'</span>, city: <span class="token-string">'Reims'</span>, region: <span class="token-string">'Grand Est'</span>, country: <span class="token-string">'France'</span>},
]</code></pre>
    </section>

    <section class="content-card" aria-labelledby="icons-heading">
        <h2 id="icons-heading">Option icons</h2>
        <p>Set <code>icon</code> on each option to show an icon beside its label in suggestions and selected tags. The component accepts several icon sources; you can mix them in one options array. <code>icon-position="start"</code> places them before labels, and <code>icon-position="end"</code> places them after. In mixed suggestion lists, options without icons reserve the same slot to keep their labels aligned. Lists with no icons do not reserve extra space.</p>
        <div class="table-scroll table-scroll--wide" role="region" aria-label="Icon formats" tabindex="0">
            <table>
                <thead><tr><th>Source</th><th>Option value</th><th>How it works</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td>Web Awesome icon</td><td><code>icon: 'location-dot'</code></td><td>Uses the default Web Awesome icon library. A descriptor such as <code>{name: 'house', family: 'classic', variant: 'solid'}</code> sets the icon properties explicitly. See <a href="https://webawesome.com/docs/components/icon"><code>wa-icon</code></a>.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Local SVG or PNG</td><td><code>icon: '/assets/icons/home.svg'</code></td><td>A string ending in <code>.svg</code> or <code>.png</code> is rendered as an image.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Remote SVG or PNG</td><td><code>icon: 'https://flagcdn.io/fr.svg'</code></td><td>Pass the image URL directly when it ends in <code>.svg</code> or <code>.png</code>.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Blob, data, or extensionless URL</td><td><code>icon: {src: imageUrl, fallback: '🇫🇷'}</code></td><td>Use an image descriptor when the URL has no file extension, or when you want fallback text if image loading fails.</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
        <p>Here the options use different formats together. For a URL from a remote API, map its image URL to <code>{src}</code> and provide optional fallback text:</p>
        <pre data-language="JavaScript"><code>field.options = [
  {<span class="token-property">value</span>: <span class="token-string">'paris'</span>, <span class="token-property">label</span>: <span class="token-string">'Paris'</span>, <span class="token-property">icon</span>: <span class="token-string">'location-dot'</span>},
  {<span class="token-property">value</span>: <span class="token-string">'home'</span>, <span class="token-property">label</span>: <span class="token-string">'Home'</span>, <span class="token-property">icon</span>: <span class="token-string">'/assets/icons/home.svg'</span>},
  {<span class="token-property">value</span>: <span class="token-string">'france'</span>, <span class="token-property">label</span>: <span class="token-string">'France'</span>, <span class="token-property">icon</span>: {<span class="token-property">src</span>: <span class="token-string">'https://flagcdn.io/fr.svg'</span>, <span class="token-property">fallback</span>: <span class="token-string">'🇫🇷'</span>}},
]

field.searchOptions = <span class="token-keyword">async</span> (query, {signal}) <span class="token-operator">=&gt;</span> {
  <span class="token-keyword">const</span> response = <span class="token-keyword">await</span> fetch(<span class="token-string">'/api/search?q='</span> + encodeURIComponent(query), {signal})
  <span class="token-keyword">const</span> results = <span class="token-keyword">await</span> response.json()
  <span class="token-keyword">return</span> results.map(item <span class="token-operator">=&gt;</span> ({
    <span class="token-property">value</span>: item.id,
    <span class="token-property">label</span>: item.name,
    <span class="token-property">icon</span>: item.iconUrl
      ? {<span class="token-property">src</span>: item.iconUrl, <span class="token-property">fallback</span>: item.iconEmoji}
      : <span class="token-string">'location-dot'</span>,
  }))
}</code></pre>
        <p>For files bundled by Vite, <a href="https://vite.dev/guide/features#glob-import">Vite glob imports</a> resolve SVG/PNG files to URLs. The autocomplete component itself does not depend on Vite.</p>
        <pre data-language="JavaScript"><code><span class="token-keyword">const</span> iconUrls = import.meta.glob(<span class="token-string">'./icons/*.{svg,png}'</span>, {
  <span class="token-property">eager</span>: <span class="token-literal">true</span>,
  <span class="token-property">import</span>: <span class="token-string">'default'</span>,
  <span class="token-property">query</span>: <span class="token-string">'?url'</span>,
})
field.options = Object.entries(iconUrls).map(([path, src]) <span class="token-operator">=&gt;</span> ({
  <span class="token-property">value</span>: path,
  <span class="token-property">label</span>: path.split(<span class="token-string">'/'</span>).pop(),
  <span class="token-property">icon</span>: {<span class="token-property">src</span>},
}))</code></pre>
    </section>

    <section class="content-card" aria-labelledby="slots-heading">
        <h2 id="slots-heading">Input slots</h2>
        <p>Use the <code>start</code> and <code>end</code> slots for fixed content inside the input, such as a search icon. Slots decorate the input; they do not set icons for individual suggestions. For those, use the option's <code>icon</code> property. The disclosure button remains in the end area.</p>
        <pre data-language="HTML"><code><span class="token-punctuation">&lt;</span><span class="token-tag">lgs1920-autocomplete</span> <span class="token-attribute">label</span>=<span class="token-attribute-value">"City"</span> <span class="token-attribute">placeholder</span>=<span class="token-attribute-value">"Search cities"</span><span class="token-punctuation">&gt;</span>
    <span class="token-punctuation">&lt;</span><span class="token-tag">wa-icon</span> <span class="token-attribute">slot</span>=<span class="token-attribute-value">"start"</span> <span class="token-attribute">name</span>=<span class="token-attribute-value">"magnifying-glass"</span> <span class="token-attribute">aria-hidden</span>=<span class="token-attribute-value">"true"</span><span class="token-punctuation">&gt;&lt;/</span><span class="token-tag">wa-icon</span><span class="token-punctuation">&gt;</span>
<span class="token-punctuation">&lt;/</span><span class="token-tag">lgs1920-autocomplete</span><span class="token-punctuation">&gt;</span></code></pre>
    </section>

    <section class="content-card" aria-labelledby="persistence-heading">
        <h2 id="persistence-heading">Recent selections</h2>
        <p>Use a stable, unique id for an independent history, or set the same group on multiple components to share recent selections. The browser stores selected option objects as JSON in <code>localStorage</code>, and shows the last selected items when the query is empty. With no recent selections, the panel stays closed instead of listing every option. Only a user selection updates the history.</p>
        <pre data-language="JavaScript"><code>field.persistence = {<span class="token-property">id</span>: <span class="token-string">'city-search'</span>, <span class="token-property">limit</span>: <span class="token-number">5</span>}

firstField.persistence = {<span class="token-property">group</span>: <span class="token-string">'location-search'</span>, <span class="token-property">limit</span>: <span class="token-number">5</span>}
secondField.persistence = {<span class="token-property">group</span>: <span class="token-string">'location-search'</span>, <span class="token-property">limit</span>: <span class="token-number">5</span>}

<span class="token-comment">// The count alias is also accepted:</span>
field.persistence = {<span class="token-property">id</span>: <span class="token-string">'city-search'</span>, <span class="token-property">count</span>: <span class="token-number">5</span>}</code></pre>
        <p>Changing the id when no group is set, or changing the group, loads a separate history. When both are set, group determines the shared history. Reducing the limit removes older entries; raising it later cannot restore removed entries. Browser storage or JSON serialization failures emit <code>wa-persistence-error</code> with <code>{error, action, id, group?}</code>.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="content-card" aria-labelledby="styling-heading">
        <h2 id="styling-heading">Styling</h2>
        <div class="table-scroll table-scroll--wide" role="region" aria-label="Styling variables" tabindex="0">
            <table>
                <thead><tr><th>CSS custom property</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td><code>--lgs1920-autocomplete-max-height</code></td><td><code>16rem</code></td><td>Maximum height of the suggestion panel.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>--lgs1920-autocomplete-placeholder-color</code></td><td><code>var(--wa-color-text-quiet)</code></td><td>Input placeholder color.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>--lgs1920-autocomplete-panel-background</code></td><td><code>var(--wa-color-surface-raised)</code></td><td>Suggestion and selected-options panel background.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>--lgs1920-autocomplete-panel-color</code></td><td><code>var(--wa-color-text-normal)</code></td><td>Suggestion and selected-options panel text color.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>--lgs1920-autocomplete-panel-border-color</code></td><td><code>var(--wa-color-surface-border)</code></td><td>Suggestion and selected-options panel border color.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>--lgs1920-autocomplete-option-color</code></td><td><code>var(--wa-color-text-normal)</code></td><td>Option text color.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>--lgs1920-autocomplete-option-icon-color</code></td><td><code>var(--wa-color-text-quiet)</code></td><td>Option icon color.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>--lgs1920-autocomplete-option-active-background</code></td><td><code>var(--wa-color-neutral-fill-quiet)</code></td><td>Keyboard-active option background.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>--lgs1920-autocomplete-option-hover-background</code></td><td><code>var(--wa-color-neutral-fill-quiet)</code></td><td>Pointer-hover option background.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>--lgs1920-autocomplete-option-selected-background</code></td><td><code>var(--wa-color-brand-fill-quiet)</code></td><td>Selected option background.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>--lgs1920-autocomplete-option-selected-color</code></td><td><code>var(--wa-color-brand-on-quiet)</code></td><td>Selected option text color.</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
        <p>The component follows the active Web Awesome theme by default. Blend an accent token with the active surface to tint individual states while preserving light and dark themes.</p>
        <pre data-language="CSS"><code>lgs1920-autocomplete {
    /* Keep the suggestion panel on the active theme surface. */
    --lgs1920-autocomplete-panel-background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--wa-color-surface-raised) 88%, var(--wa-color-purple) 12%);
    /* Follow the active theme's foreground color. */
    --lgs1920-autocomplete-panel-color: var(--wa-color-text-normal);
    /* Tint hovered options without replacing the theme surface. */
    --lgs1920-autocomplete-option-hover-background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--wa-color-surface-raised) 86%, var(--wa-color-purple) 14%);
    /* Keep selected text readable on the tinted surface. */
    --lgs1920-autocomplete-option-selected-background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--wa-color-surface-raised) 68%, var(--wa-color-purple) 32%);
    /* Follow the active theme's foreground color. */
    --lgs1920-autocomplete-option-selected-color: var(--wa-color-text-normal);
}</code></pre>
    </section>

    <section class="content-card" aria-labelledby="remote-heading">
        <h2 id="remote-heading">Remote API example</h2>
        <p>The callback receives an abort signal. Forward it to <code>fetch</code> so the browser can stop obsolete requests as the query changes.</p>
        <pre data-language="JavaScript"><code>field.searchOptions = <span class="token-keyword">async</span> (query, {signal}) <span class="token-operator">=&gt;</span> {
  <span class="token-keyword">const</span> response = <span class="token-keyword">await</span> fetch(<span class="token-string">`/api/cities?q=${encodeURIComponent(query)}`</span>, {signal})
  <span class="token-keyword">if</span> (!response.ok) <span class="token-keyword">throw</span> <span class="token-keyword">new</span> Error(<span class="token-string">'City search failed'</span>)
  <span class="token-keyword">return</span> response.json()
}</code></pre>
        <p>The endpoint should return an array in the documented option shape. The live city example uses <a href="https://photon.komoot.io/">Photon</a>, filters results to cities, and maps each result to a stable OpenStreetMap identifier plus its coordinates and country metadata. Photon’s public demo server is intended for reasonable request volumes and does not provide an availability guarantee. A failed request shows a status message and emits <code>wa-search-error</code>. The selected value participates in form submission and is cleared when the owning form resets.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="content-card" aria-labelledby="events-heading">
        <h2 id="events-heading">Events</h2>
        <div class="table-scroll table-scroll--wide" role="region" aria-label="Component events" tabindex="0">
            <table>
                <thead><tr><th>Event</th><th>Detail</th><th>When</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td><code>input</code></td><td>Standard component event</td><td>Whenever the user edits the query. Read its text from <code>event.target.query</code>.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>change</code></td><td>Standard component event</td><td>When the selected value changes or the input value is committed. Read the selected value from <code>event.target.value</code>.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>focus</code> / <code>blur</code></td><td>Standard component events</td><td>When the underlying input receives or loses focus.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>wa-clear</code></td><td>Custom component event</td><td>When the query-clear or clear-all control is activated.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>wa-select</code></td><td><code>{option, value, label, selectedOptions}</code></td><td>After a suggestion is selected. In multiple mode, <code>value</code> is an array.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>wa-deselect</code></td><td><code>{option, value, label, selectedOptions}</code></td><td>When a selected option is toggled off in multiple mode.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>wa-search-error</code></td><td><code>{error, query}</code></td><td>When a current async search fails.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>wa-option-render-error</code></td><td><code>{error, option}</code></td><td>When <code>renderOption</code> throws, returns something other than a DOM node, or <code>optionTemplate</code> cannot be rendered. The default label view is used for that suggestion.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>wa-option-template-error</code></td><td><code>{error, templateId}</code></td><td>When the <code>option-template</code> attribute does not reference an HTML <code>&lt;template&gt;</code> element in the same document.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>wa-persistence-error</code></td><td><code>{error, action, id, group?}</code></td><td>When browser storage cannot be read or written. For a group-only configuration, <code>id</code> contains the group name.</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
    </section>

